  "name": "Fort Worth Livestock Exchange Building",
  "scope": "Whole surviving named Livestock Exchange Building at131EastExchangeAvenue, the Stockyards central landmark: original full21vertexT-shaped outer plan and both six-vertex internal open courtyards; pale cream/straw stucco, terracotta tiled hipped/gabled roofs and broad eaves, genuine south/front open round-arch arcade on square piers, taller central second-storey Mission Revival scalloped/stepped parapet with ball finials, central shingled square cupola with arched sash/bellcast patinated metal roof/small louvred lantern/cap/finial and own entry steps, plus connected rear office/auction wing. Exclude entire Stockyards district/cattlepens, detached CowtownColiseum/StockyardsHotel/station/barns, roads/parking/plazas/landscape/statues/signage/lettering/longhorn-headartwork/interiors/animals/people/cars and separateflagpoles. No historical demolished packingplant reconstruction.",
  "era": "Surviving permanent Livestock Exchange architecture from exact2012and earlierHighsmithpublic-domain exteriors plus original current full multipolygon plan. Current cosmetics/renovations, concealed roof partition/rear elevations and source heights remain bounded estimates; not whole district reconstruction.",
